From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:51:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] libcameraservice: hand HAL1 recording frames back off
 the callback thread

In buffer-queue video mode CameraClient copied each recording frame into
the video target and then released it to the HAL from inside
handleGenericDataTimestamp(), on the HAL's data callback thread. That
deadlocked QCamera2 (msm8916, the Galaxy A3 2015) in two ways:

- The release took mLock again. stopRecording() holds mLock across
  mHardware->stopRecording(), which on QCamera2 joins exactly that
  callback thread (QCameraChannel::stop() -> QCameraCmdThread::exit() ->
  pthread_join), so each waited for the other for good.
- Without mLock, the release is still a nested HIDL call made from
  inside the provider's callback, which binder runs on that same
  provider thread. stopRecording() holds the HIDL CameraDevice's lock
  while it joins the thread, so the nested release waited for the lock
  and the join waited for the release.

Either way the camera stayed wedged until minimediaservice restarted.

The callback now reads the mode and takes a reference to the hardware
interface while mLock is still held, and queues the release for a
CamFrameRelease thread instead of making it. The callback returns at
once, the join completes and the release follows. disconnect() and the
destructor stop the thread before mHardware->release(); it first hands
back everything still queued. A frame that arrives after that is
dropped with a warning: the HAL frees its buffers anyway.

Tested on the Galaxy A3 (2015): 100/100 cycles of the camcycle soak
(preview, pictures, hardware recording, close while recording, both
cameras). Built for halium_arm64 and halium_arm with -Werror. clang
--analyze (alpha unix/security/core/cplusplus checkers), clang-tidy,
cppcheck and flawfinder report nothing on the new lines; what they
report is all in the file without this change too. There is no unit
test for the HAL1 CameraClient to extend.

Change-Id: Ic2d9e94873806ffe713c28aaa274fdd5870d1e5f
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
